decisions:
  - id: unified-action-enum
    decision: Route all inputs through a single ConductorAction enum
    rationale: Decouples input sources from action execution. Any input (eyebrow, gesture, voice command, custom gesture) maps to the same action type, making the system composable and user-configurable.
  - id: pure-struct-state-machines
    decision: EyebrowStateMachine is a pure value-type struct with a @MainActor wrapper class
    rationale: Pure structs are trivially testable (no async, no setup). The wrapper class handles @MainActor isolation and @Published state for SwiftUI. Pattern reused from existing GestureStateMachine.
  - id: dtw-over-euclidean
    decision: Use Dynamic Time Warping for custom gesture matching instead of simple Euclidean distance
    rationale: Hand gestures have variable duration — DTW handles time-warped sequences. A wave at 0.5x speed should still match a template recorded at 1x speed.
  - id: edge-only-voice-commands
    decision: Only detect voice commands at the start or end of transcription text
    rationale: Prevents false positives from mid-sentence matches. 'I want to send an email' should not trigger the 'send' command.
  - id: sidebar-dual-mode
    decision: ConductorPanel supports both sidebar and floating overlay modes
    rationale: Backward compatibility for users who prefer the floating overlay. Sidebar is the new default for workspace management but the old mode is preserved.
  - id: mainactor-appdelegate
    decision: Made entire AppDelegate class @MainActor
    rationale: All AppDelegate methods interact with UI (NSPanel, NSStatusBar, WorkspaceManager). Annotating the class is simpler and correct vs annotating each method individually.
errors_encountered:
  - description: EyebrowEvent failed OSLog interpolation — 'appendInterpolation requires CustomStringConvertible'
    resolution: Added CustomStringConvertible conformance with description computed property
    time_to_fix: 1min
  - description: CGFloat.greatestFiniteMagnitude ambiguous between CoreFoundation.CGFloat and Swift.Double
    resolution: Qualified as CGFloat.greatestFiniteMagnitude explicitly
    time_to_fix: 1min
  - description: Missing self. in string interpolations inside closures (3 files)
    resolution: Added self. prefix in ConductorPanel, CustomGestureClassifier, and WorkspaceManager
    time_to_fix: 2min
  - description: AppDelegate launchPanel accessing @MainActor WorkspaceManager properties from non-isolated context
    resolution: Made AppDelegate class @MainActor, removed redundant @MainActor annotations on properties
    time_to_fix: 3min
  - description: Unused variable warning for previousState in EyebrowStateMachine
    resolution: Removed the unused variable
    time_to_fix: 1min
learnings:
  - OSLog string interpolation requires CustomStringConvertible conformance on custom enum types — Swift compiler error is not intuitive ('appendInterpolation requires conformance')
  - CGFloat.greatestFiniteMagnitude is ambiguous in NSSize context because both CGFloat and Double have the property — must qualify explicitly
  - Swift 6 strict concurrency requires explicit self. in string interpolations inside closures, even for @MainActor classes — this catches many files at once
  - Making NSApplicationDelegate subclasses @MainActor resolves most actor isolation issues since all their methods touch UI anyway
  - AsyncStream with [weak self] capture + Task { @MainActor in } is the standard pattern for safe continuation storage across the codebase
  - MediaPipe FaceMesh Python subprocess output format can be extended with backward compatibility by checking parts.count in the Swift parser
  - DTW sliding window matching needs buffer clearing after a match to prevent repeated triggers of the same gesture
